  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">- The Labour Advisory Council is established by Ministerial Decree of 26 May 2021; 
- Regulation for the Establishment, Organization and Rules of Functioning of the Labour Advisory Council of the Republic of South Sudan adopted on 5 July 2021;
- LAC members appointed by Ministerial Decree of 26 May 2021;
- LAC established as mandated by Article 20 of the Labour Act, making explicit reference to &quot;Advise the Office of the Labour Commissioner on issues arising from the activities of 
the International Labour Organization&quot;


 - ILO developed TOR for international consultant;
- Consultant drafted Regulations and Rules with technical assistance of ILO NPC South Sudan, CO Addis Ababa, DWT for North Africa and headquarters;
- ILO organized and technically facilitated tripartite workshop discussing and approving draft regulation on 31 May and 1 June 2021</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.2 Number of member States with tripartite mechanisms enabling constituents to effectively engage in the implementation of international labour standards at the national level, including reporting to the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Strengthened social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In June 2021, the Ministry of Labour of South Sudan adopted a regulation for the establishment of the Labour Advisory Council (LAC) . The regulation has been validated by the tripartite constituents in a workshop organized from 30 May to 1 June 2021. ILO technical assistance were key in achieving the objectives.  A tripartite workshop on the drafting of the regulations specifying the mandate and functioning of the LAC was facilitated by the ILO on May 31 and June 1 2021. The final version of these regulations is validated by the constituents.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.4.1. Number of member States with newly developed or strengthened institutions, mechanisms or regulatory frameworks for social dialogue, labour relations or dispute prevention/resolution that address current and emerging challenges in the world of work</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
